## Mission

Break the OpenRouter generation-404 deadlock without fabricating a zero bill, dropping historical liability, regenerating retained answers, or widening financial authority.

## Mechanism

When the exact interrupted generation still returns provider HTTP 404:
- retain actual cost as UNKNOWN / null;
- quarantine the full pre-call `reservedWorstCaseUsd` as conservative economic liability;
- retain semantic authority NONE;
- preserve failed state and sealed ciphertext;
- allow the continuation checkpoint to be recovered only if the quarantine is internally consistent;
- never count the vanished response as candidate evidence;
- revalidate every other historical provider bill exactly;
- charge the quarantined liability against both the $0.45 evaluation envelope and protected Crown reserve.

Only the one missing Sol answer and one evaluator call remain eligible after separate owner authorization.

## No authority created

This patch performs no paid inference, creates no R3 owner authorization, and does not mint a Crown admission. Existing monthly runtime authority is not treated as retry authority.

OpenRouter support ticket #116019 remains external evidence lineage.

