This PR:
- adds an additive idempotent migration for `outbound_events.provider_event_id`;
- gives each frozen effect a deterministic Message-ID before provider dispatch;
- logs a minimal sanitized provider-result reconciliation checkpoint immediately after provider return;
- commits the provider receipt/effect-cap checkpoint in its own transaction before secondary reservation/event-ledger reconciliation;
- returns an explicit non-retry reconciliation state instead of losing the provider result if later persistence fails;
- adds a regression that forces the post-provider outbound-event ledger to fail and proves the provider receipt survives, effect cap remains zero, and replay is denied.

